## 9. Command Term Quick Guide

| Command Term | What to Do | Typical Answer Style |
|---|---|---|
| State | give a short answer | one word or one sentence |
| Identify | name the correct item | short phrase |
| Outline | give a brief point with small detail | 1-2 sentences |
| Describe | give characteristics or details | clear explanation |
| Explain | give reason, cause, effect, or how | point + because/how |
| Compare | give similarities and differences | structured contrast |
| Discuss | balanced review, different sides | advantages, disadvantages, conclusion |
| Evaluate | judge strengths and weaknesses | balanced judgement |
| Suggest | propose a suitable answer | idea + reason |
| Justify | give reasons for a choice | choice + evidence |
| Construct | create algorithm/diagram/code | complete working answer |
| Trace | follow and record values | table or step-by-step values |
| Sketch | draw approximate structure | labelled diagram |

---

## 10. Answer Length Guide

| Marks | Expected Depth |
|---:|---|
| 1 mark | one correct point |
| 2 marks | one point with expansion OR two short points |
| 3 marks | several linked points OR point + expansion + scenario |
| 4 marks | usually two developed points |
| 5-6 marks | structured answer with detail and scenario links |
| 8+ marks | longer answer, balanced discussion, clear structure |
| 12 marks | developed analysis, context, balance, conclusion if required |

### Important

Do not write a huge paragraph for a 1-mark question.  
Do not write one vague sentence for a 6-mark question.

